<title>GERMANY: Daimler adds Saturday shifts for Mercedes.</title>
<headline>Daimler adds Saturday shifts for Mercedes.</headline>
<dateline>STUTTGART, Germany 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's Daimler-Benz AG said on Thursday it has agreed with its works council on additional Saturday shifts for two of its Mercedes vehicle plants.</p>
<p>Daimler said the additional shifts have been agreed to for workers at a passenger vehicle plant in Sindelfingen and a vehicle engine factory in Untertuerkheim.</p>
<p>A Daimler spokesman said eight Saturday shifts would take place at each plant between September and December.</p>
<p>Daimler has said it wants to build over 700,000 passenger vehicles in 1997 compared with 645,000 vehicles in 1996. Daimler officials said the additional Saturday shifts were needed to help reach the production goal.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
